oding, bounded binding/corruption recovery, epic-only hierarchy, two-pass unbound-parent grace, conflict/dedup/status/deletion semantics, bounded convergence, cleanup/restore, and positive status-propagation behavior.\n- `scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_validation_probe.sh` — Preserve manual opt-in, `--only` scoping, CLI event-store writes, portable filtered counts, bounded settling, preview-cleanliness checks, conflict-policy title tolerance, and Jira/local cleanup.\n\nConsumers are hook settings/docs/tests and the manual Jira pressure-test guide. Preserve exact `# shellcheck disable=SC2329 # invoked via trap` and all `# tickets-boundary-ok` sanctions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The leaf commit changes only comments/docstrings or blank lines in the four declared files; exact directives remain.\n- [x] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [x] Every edited block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row showing bloat removal with current rationale retained.\n- [x] Focused hook/pressure-test checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass; no missing or FAIL semantic row remains.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, focused tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/_backtest/__init__.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/hooks/serena_grep_reminder.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_field_validation_probe.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_validation_probe.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3de8-31a0-25ef-456d"],["relates_to","0f7d-aad8-5fe8-42fb"],["relates_to","ed99-9ad3-d425-44bc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3de8-31a0-25ef-456d","parent_status_uuid":"189131e8-6928-4b2c-a16b-68fce0c3bb83","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"3666-6209-1783-47a2","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in scripts — cohort 01: init__–e2e_validation_probe","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import ast, subprocess, sys\ndef norm(ref, path):\n    src = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{ref}:{path}\"], text=True)\n    tree = ast.parse(src, type_comments=True)\n    for ti in tree.type_ignores:\n        ti.lineno = 0\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        body = getattr(node, \"body\", None)\n        if isinstance(body, list) and body and isinstance(body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(body[0].value.value, str):\n            node.body = body[1:]\n    return ast.dump(tree, include_attributes=False)\nbad = [p for p in sys.argv[1:] if norm(\"HEAD^\", p) != norm(\"HEAD\", p)]\nassert not bad, f\"non-prose AST changes: {bad}\"' scripts/_backtest/__init__.py scripts/hooks/serena_grep_reminder.py","dd_id":"python-prose-only","dd_text":"Compare Python ASTs after removing docstrings and normalizing TypeIgnore line numbers so only comments/docstrings may differ."},{"command":"rtk git diff --exit-code --ignore-matching-lines=\"^\\([[:space:]]*#[^!].*\\|[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*\\|[[:space:]]*;.*\\|[[:space:]]*<!--.*\\|[[:space:]]*.*-->\\|[[:space:]]*\\)$\" HEAD^ HEAD -- scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_field_validation_probe.sh scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2